O|
O|                                                                            ii   
O|
O|                              ‘Life, to be sure,                                    
O|                               Is nothing much to lose,                             
O|                               But young men think it is,                           
O|                               And we were young.’                                  
O|
O|                                        -A.E. Housman                               
O|
O|                 ‘We have so much to say, and we shall never say it.’               
O|
O|                                        -Erich Maria Remarque                       
O|                                        All Quiet On The Western Front              
O|
O|
O|                                                                           iii  
O|
M|                                         NOTE:                                      
M|          The following script takes place in real time, and - with the             
M|          exception of one moment - is written and designed to be one single        
M|          continuous shot.                                                          
O|
O|
O|                                                                     1.          
O|
S|               EXT. MEADOW - DAY, APRIL 6TH 1917                                    
N|               A rolling landscape. The rustling of leaves, and birdsong.           
O|
N|               Thunder rumbles in the distance. There is no rain.                   
O|
N|               A figure lies against a tree, eyes closed - this is                  
N,I|               SCHOFIELD, early-20s. Soft features.                                 
O|
N,I|               A man is sleeping next to him on the grass - BLAKE, 19,              
N,I|               youthful, strapping.                                                 
O|
C,E|                                   SERGEANT SANDERS (O.S.)                          
U|                         Blake.                                                     
N|               Blake doesn’t stir.                                                  
O|
C,E|                                   SERGEANT SANDERS (O.S.) (CONT'D)                 
U|                         Blake!                                                     
O|
N|               Blake wakes. He’s in uniform, damp and crumpled - Lance              
N|               Corporal chevrons adorn it.                                          
O|
C|                                   BLAKE                                            
P|                             (sleepily)                                             
U|                         Sorry, Sarge.                                              
C|                                   SERGEANT SANDERS                                 
U|                         Pick a man, bring your kit.                                
O|
C|                                   BLAKE                                            
U|                         Yes, Sarge.                                                
O|
N|               Blake stands, stiff limbs coming back to life.                       
O|
N|               Schofield’s eyes are still shut. Blake holds out his hand to         
N|               Schofield. Schofield opens his eyes - they are gentle, wise.         
N|               Schofield grudgingly raises his hand for a lift.                     
O|
N|               Blake heaves him to his feet - his uniform is identical to           
N|               Blake’s, same rank, the only difference is the brass wound           
N|               stripe on Schofield’s left sleeve.                                   
N|               They trudge towards Sanders, fastening their webbing. A              
N|               smattering of SOLDIERS - same regiment - same state of               
N|               fatigue and filth, lie around them. Stealing sleep.                  
O|
C,E|                                   SERGEANT SANDERS (O.S.)                          
U|                         Don’t dawdle.                                              
O|
C|                                   BLAKE                                            
U|                         No, Sarge.                                                 
O|
O|                                                                (CONTINUED)
O|
O|
O|                                                                     2.          
O|
O|               CONTINUED:                                                
O|
N|               After a few paces the long grass begins to give way to well          
N|               trodden earth. Washing lines appears on either side of them.         
N|               Blake and Schofield move past them. After a while -                  
O|
C,E|                                   BLAKE (CONT'D)                                   
U|                         Did they feed us?                                          
O|
N|               Schofield shakes his head, he hands an envelope to Blake.            
O|
C|                                   SCHOFIELD                                        
U|                         No, just mail.                                             
O|
N|               Blake’s eyes light up at the sight of the envelope, he tears         
N|               it open, reads it as he walks. Eyes scanning quickly, his            
N|               face filling with warmth.                                            
C|                                   BLAKE                                            
P|                             (reading)                                              
U|                         Myrtle’s having puppies.                                   
O|
N|               Blake finishes the note and slips it into a pocket.                  
O|
C,E|                                   BLAKE (CONT'D)                                   
U|                         You get anything?                                          
O|
C|                                   SCHOFIELD                                        
U|                         No.                                                        
N|               Schofield doesn’t seem to mind.                                      
O|
N|               The mess tents are now alongside. Fires are stoked, cooking          
N|               is underway. More soldiers mill about.                               
O|
C|                                   BLAKE                                            
U|                         I’m bloody starving, aren’t you? I                         
U|                         thought we might get some decent                           
U|                         grub out here - only reason I                              
U|                         decided against the priesthood.                            
N|               Schofield lets out a laugh. Blake looks on hungrily as they          
N|               pass by the mess tents.                                              
O|
N|               Schofield rummages in his pockets, finds what he’s looking           
N|               for - a handkerchief with some food wrapped in it. Blake’s           
N|               eyes fall on it hungrily.                                            
O|
C,E|                                   BLAKE (CONT'D)                                   
U|                         What you got there?                                        
O|
C|                                   SCHOFIELD                                        
U|                         Ham and bread.                                             
O|
O|                                                                (CONTINUED)
O|
O|
O|                                                                     3.          
O|
O|               CONTINUED: (2)                                         
O|
C|                                   BLAKE                                            
U|                         Where did you find that?                                   
C|                                   SCHOFIELD                                        
U|                         I have my uses.                                            
O|
N|               Schofield breaks the bread in half. As he does this, they            
N|               move down a slope, and begin to descend down into the earth,         
N|               into--                                                               
O|
S|               EXT. COMMS TRENCH - DAY - CONTINUOUS                                 
O|
N|               A narrow Comms trench.                                               
C|                                   SCHOFIELD                                        
U|                         Here-                                                      
O|
N|               The bread is stale, practically cardboard. Blake’s teeth             
N|               struggle to get through it.                                          
O|
C|                                   BLAKE                                            
P|                             (mouth full of food)                                   
U|                         Tastes like old shoe.                                      
O|
C|                                   SCHOFIELD                                        
U|                         Cheer up. This time next week it’ll                        
U|                         be chicken dinner.                                         
N|               The trench drops deeper into the earth...                            
O|
C|                                   BLAKE                                            
U|                         Not me. Leave got cancelled.                               
O|
C|                                   SCHOFIELD                                        
U|                         They say why?                                              
O|
C|                                   BLAKE                                            
U|                         No idea.                                                   
N|               A beat. The world above has now disappeared.                         
O|
C|                                   SCHOFIELD                                        
U|                         It’s easier not to go back at all.                         
O|
N|               Blake registers this - looks at him.                                 
O|
N|               The wider Rear Trench crosses their path. Chains of soldiers         
N|               move past them - shifting crates, ammunition, cooking, and           
N|               medical supplies.                                                    
O|
O|                                                                (CONTINUED)
O|
O|
O|                                                                     4.          
O|
O|               CONTINUED:                                                
O|
C|                                   BLAKE                                            
P|                             (looking at the soldiers)                              
U|                         Something’s up.                                            
N|               Expectation is growing in Blake. But Schofield looks                 
N|               concerned. They cut a route through the bustle.                      
O|
C,E|                                   BLAKE (CONT'D)                                   
U|                         Did you hear anything?                                     
O|
C|                                   SCHOFIELD                                        
U|                         No.                                                        
O|
C|                                   BLAKE                                            
U|                         Has to be the push, right?                                 
N|               Men carrying things push past them. Blake watches.                   
O|
C,E|                                   BLAKE (CONT'D)                                   
U|                         Ten bob says we’re going up.                               
O|
C|                                   SCHOFIELD                                        
U|                         I’m not taking that bet.                                   
O|
C|                                   BLAKE                                            
U|                         Why? ‘Cos you know I’m right?                              
C|                                   SCHOFIELD                                        
U|                         No. ‘Cos you haven’t got ten bob.                          
O|
N|               Blake laughs.                                                        
O|
N|               They follow Sanders into-                                            
O|
S|               EXT. SECOND TRENCH - CONTINUOUS                                      
O|
N|               They turn into a wider second line trench.                           
O|
C|                                   SERGEANT SANDERS                                 
U|                         In your own time, gentlemen...                             
N|               Up ahead, Sanders waits.                                             
O|
N|               Blake and Schofield put on speed, catch Sanders.                     
O|
C|                                   BLAKE                                            
U|                         Is there news, Sarge?                                      
O|
C|                                   SERGEANT SANDERS                                 
U|                         News of what?                                              
O|
O|                                                                (CONTINUED)
O|
O|
O|                                                                     5.          
O|
O|               CONTINUED:                                                
O|
C|                                   BLAKE                                            
U|                         The big push. It was supposed to                           
U|                         happen weeks ago. They told us we’d                        
U|                         be home by Christmas.                                      
C|                                   SERGEANT SANDERS                                 
P|                             (mild sarcasm)                                         
U|                         Yes, well, sorry to disrupt your                           
U|                         crowded schedule, Blake, but the                           
U|                         Brass Hats didn’t fancy it in the                          
U|                         snow.                                                      
O|
C|                                   BLAKE                                            
U|                         More’s the pity Sarge, I could have                        
U|                         done with some turkey.                                     
C|                                   SERGEANT SANDERS                                 
U|                         Well, I’ll make sure to relay your                         
U|                         displeasure to command.                                    
O|
N|               Ahead and above them is a web of telegraph wires - stretching        
N|               overhead and along the trench. THREE ROYAL ENGINEERS are             
N|               working on them, tagging and testing. They duck around them.         
O|
C|                                   SCHOFIELD                                        
U|                         So what’s on the cards then,                               
U|                         Sergeant?                                                  
C|                                   SERGEANT SANDERS                                 
U|                         The Hun are up to something.                               
O|
C|                                   SCHOFIELD                                        
U|                         Any idea what?                                             
O|
C|                                   SERGEANT SANDERS                                 
U|                         No - but it’s bound to ruin our                            
U|                         weekend.                                                   
O|
N|               Sanders turns a corner, and comes to a stop. Just beyond him         
N|               is the dark, yawning mouth of a Dugout.                              
C,E|                                   SERGEANT SANDERS (CONT'D)                        
U|                         Now listen, Erinmore is inside, so                         
U|                         tidy yourselves up.                                        
O|
N|               They are suddenly alert.                                             
O|
C,E|                                   SERGEANT SANDERS (CONT'D)                        
U|                         You never know - might be mentions                         
U|                         in dispatches for this one, if you                         
U|                         don’t bugger it up.                                        
O|
O|                                                                (CONTINUED)
O|
O|
O|                                                                     6.          
O|
O|               CONTINUED: (2)                                         
O|
N|               Sanders gives them a look, and disappears inside the dugout.         
N|               Schofield quickly buttons up his tunic, hiding any sins there        
N|               may be underneath.                                                   
O|
N|               Blake nervously tidies himself, leans in to Schofield.               
O|
C|                                   BLAKE                                            
U|                         Must be something big if the                               
U|                         General’s here.                                            
O|
N|               They enter.                                                          
O|
S|               INT. DUGOUT - CONTINUOUS                                             
O|
N|               Lit by paraffin lamps, it takes Schofield a moment for his           
N|               eyes to adjust to the half-light. He and Blake hand their            
N|               rifles to the ORDERLIES, salute, and stand at attention.             
O|
N|               There is a simmering sense of unease in this place.                  
O|
N|               In the centre of the room, there are two tables. On one table        
N|               lie several maps, on the other are a number of large aerial          
N|               reconnaissance photographs.                                          
O|
M,I|               GENERAL ERINMORE (50s), LIEUTENANT GORDON (40s) and a CAPTAIN        
N|               are gathered around the far table, looking down at the               
N|               aerials, talking in hushed tones.                                    
N|               Other men watch from the shadows - TWO NCOs and ANOTHER              
N|               ORDERLY.                                                             
O|
C|                                   SERGEANT SANDERS                                 
U|                         Lance Corporals Blake and                                  
U|                         Schofield, Sir.                                            
O|
N|               General Erinmore turns around. Looks at Blake and Schofield.         
O|
C|                                   GENERAL ERINMORE                                 
U|                         Which one of you is Blake?                                 
C|                                   BLAKE                                            
U|                         Sir.                                                       
O|
C|                                   ERINMORE                                         
U|                         You have a brother, a Lieutenant in                        
U|                         the 2nd Devons?                                            
O|
C|                                   BLAKE                                            
U|                         Yes, sir. Joseph Blake. Is he-                             
O|
O|                                                                (CONTINUED)
O|
O|
O|                                                                     7.          
O|
O|               CONTINUED:                                                
O|
C|                                   ERINMORE                                         
U|                         Alive, as far as I know. And with                          
U|                         your help I’d like to keep it that                         
U|                         way.                                                       
N|               Blake stares at Erinmore, he would do anything.                      
O|
C,E|                                   ERINMORE (CONT'D)                                
U|                         Sanders tells me you’re good with                          
U|                         maps. That true?                                           
O|
C|                                   BLAKE                                            
U|                         Good enough, Sir.                                          
C|                                   ERINMORE                                         
U|                         So.                                                        
O|
N|               Erinmore turns the map to face Blake. The British lines are          
N|               marked in blue, the German lines in red.                             
O|
C,E|                                   ERINMORE (CONT'D)                                
U|                         We are here. The 2nd Devons are                            
U|                         advancing here.                                            
O|
N|               He points out a cross on the map at Croisilles Wood.                 
O|
C,E|                                   ERINMORE (CONT'D)                                
U|                         How long will it take you to get                           
U|                         there?                                                     
N|               Blake hesitantly studies it. Croisilles Wood sits in the             
N|               centre of a huge area of land, which is scored as occupied           
N|               territory.                                                           
O|
C|                                   BLAKE                                            
U|                         I don’t understand, Sir.                                   
O|
C|                                   SCHOFIELD                                        
U|                         Sir, that land is held by the                              
U|                         Germans.                                                   
C|                                   ERINMORE                                         
U|                         Germans have gone.                                         
O|
N|               Shock plays on their faces.                                          
O|
C,E|                                   ERINMORE (CONT'D)                                
U|                         Don’t get your hopes up. It appears                        
U|                         to be a strategic withdrawal. They                         
U|                         seem to have created a new line,                           
U|                         nine miles back here, by the looks                         
U|                         of it.                                                     
O|
O|                                                                (CONTINUED)
O|
O|
O|                                                                     8.          
O|
O|               CONTINUED: (2)                                         
O|
N|               Erinmore runs his finger along the massed red lines of the           
N|               German trenches and fortifications, newly drawn on the map.          
N|               The new German Line - what came to be known as the Hindenburg        
N|               Line - is huge, and cuts its way across the paper, almost            
N|               intersecting with Croisilles Wood.                                   
O|
C,E|                                   ERINMORE (CONT'D)                                
U|                         Colonel Mackenzie is in command of                         
U|                         the 2nd. He sent word yesterday                            
U|                         morning that he was going after the                        
U|                         retreating Germans. He is convinced                        
U|                         he has them on the run - that if he                        
U|                         can break their lines now, he will                         
U|                         turn the tide. He is wrong.                                
N|               Schofield watches Blake as he begins to register what this           
N|               might mean.                                                          
O|
C,E|                                   ERINMORE (CONT'D)                                
U|                         Colonel Mackenzie has not seen                             
U|                         these aerials of the enemy’s new                           
U|                         line.                                                      
O|
N|               Erinmore turns to the other table.                                   
O|
C,E|                                   ERINMORE (CONT'D)                                
U|                         Come round here, Gentlemen.                                
N|               Blake and Schofield move to the next table. They look down at        
N|               the large aerial photographs.                                        
O|
C,E|                                   ERINMORE (CONT'D)                                
U|                         Three miles deep. Field                                    
U|                         fortifications, defences and                               
U|                         artillery the like of which we’ve                          
U|                         never seen before.                                         
O|
N|               Beat.                                                                
C,E|                                   ERINMORE (CONT'D)                                
U|                         The 2nd are due to attack the line                         
U|                         shortly after dawn tomorrow. They                          
U|                         have no idea what they are in for.                         
U|                         And we can’t warn them - as a                              
U|                         parting gift, the enemy cut all our                        
U|                         telephone lines.                                           
O|
N|               Blake and Schofield are silent while they take this in.              
O|
O|                                                                (CONTINUED)
O|
O|
O|                                                                     9.          
O|
O|               CONTINUED: (3)                                         
O|
C,E|                                   ERINMORE (CONT'D)                                
U|                         Your orders are to get to the 2nd                          
U|                         at Croisilles Wood, one mile south                         
U|                         east of the town of Ecoust.                                
N,G|               Erinmore hands over an envelope to Blake. We see the                 
N,G|               distinctive red stamp of Army Command.                               
O|
C,E|                                   ERINMORE (CONT'D)                                
U|                         Deliver this to Colonel Mackenzie.                         
U|                         It is a direct order to call off                           
U|                         tomorrow morning’s attack.                                 
O|
N|               Erinmore speaks slowly, desperate to impress upon Blake and          
N|               Schofield the gravity of this situation. Nothing can be              
N|               misunderstood.                                                       
C,E|                                   ERINMORE (CONT'D)                                
U|                         If you don’t, it will be a                                 
U|                         massacre. We would lose two                                
U|                         battalions. Sixteen hundred men,                           
U|                         your brother among them.                                   
O|
N|               Schofield hides his shock. But Blake looks at Erinmore,              
N|               determination etched in his face: understood.                        
O|
C,E|                                   ERINMORE (CONT'D)                                
U|                         Do you think you can get there in                          
U|                         time?                                                      
C|                                   BLAKE                                            
U|                         Yes, Sir.                                                  
O|
C|                                   ERINMORE                                         
U|                         Any questions?                                             
O|
C|                                   BLAKE                                            
U|                         No, Sir.                                                   
O|
N|               Schofield eyes flick to Blake: No questions? Blake purposely         
N|               doesn’t catch Schofield’s eye.                                       
C|                                   ERINMORE                                         
U|                         Good. Over to you, Lieutenant.                             
O|
N|               The men salute Erinmore. Lieutenant Gordon, stands to one            
N|               side.                                                                
O|
C|                                   LIEUTENANT GORDON                                
U|                         Supplies, Gentlemen.                                       
O|
O|                                                                (CONTINUED)
O|
O|
O|                                                                     10.        
O|
O|               CONTINUED: (4)                                         
O|
N|               Lt. Gordon nods them over to a table. Various items are laid         
N|               out on it.                                                           
C,E|                                   LIEUTENANT GORDON (CONT'D)                       
U|                         Map, torches, grenades, and a                              
U|                         couple of little treats.                                   
O|
N|               They look. A folded map, two electric torches, two grenades          
N|               and two small packs of Huntley and Palmer biscuits lie on the        
N|               table. They take them and start hastily putting them into            
N|               their webbing. While they do:                                        
O|
C,E|                                   LIEUTENANT GORDON (CONT'D)                       
U|                         Leave immediately, take this trench                        
U|                         west, up on Sauchiehall Street,                            
U|                         then north west on Paradise Alley                          
U|                         at the front. Continue along the                           
U|                         front line until you find the                              
U|                         Yorks.                                                     
N|               Gordon slides a note into Blake’s top pocket.                        
O|
C,E|                                   LIEUTENANT GORDON (CONT'D)                       
U|                         Give this note to Major Stevenson.                         
U|                         He’s holding the line at the                               
U|                         shortest span of No Man’s Land.                            
U|                         You’ll cross there.                                        
N|               Both men turn at the mention of No Man’s Land.                       
O|
C|                                   SCHOFIELD                                        
U|                         It will be daylight, Sir. They’ll                          
U|                         see us.                                                    
O|
C,E|                                   ERINMORE (O.C.)                                  
U|                         No need to be concerned. You should                        
U|                         meet no resistance.                                        
O|
N|               An Orderly hands them back their rifles.                             
N|               Blake moves towards the doorway. Schofield turns to Erinmore.        
O|
C|                                   SCHOFIELD                                        
U|                         Sir, is it just us?                                        
O|
N|               Erinmore looks up.                                                   
O|
C|                                   ERINMORE                                         
U|                         “Down to Gehenna or up to the                              
U|                         Throne                                                     
O|                                   (MORE)                                    
O|
O|                                                                (CONTINUED)
O|
O|
O|                                                                     11.        
O|
O|               CONTINUED: (5)                                         
C,E|                                   ERINMORE (CONT'D)               
U|                         He travels the fastest who travels                         
U|                         alone.”                                                    
U|                         Wouldn’t you say, Lieutenant?                              
C|                                   LIEUTENANT GORDON                                
U|                         Yes, Sir. I would.                                         
O|
N|               The General looks at them levelly.                                   
O|
C|                                   ERINMORE                                         
U|                         Good luck.                                                 
O|
N|               Blake and Schofield turn and head through the door-                  
O|
S|               EXT. SECOND LINE TRENCH - CONTINUOUS                                 
O|
N|               Schofield’s eyes wince in the daylight. A small curved branch        
N|               leads from the rear of the dugout back to the Second Line.           
O|
C|                                   SCHOFIELD                                        
U|                         Blake - let’s talk about this for a                        
U|                         minute.                                                    
O|
C|                                   BLAKE                                            
U|                         Why?                                                       
N|               Blake is already off, moving fast.                                   
O|
N|               Schofield moves after him, trying to fill and fasten his             
N|               webbing as he goes.                                                  
O|
C|                                   SCHOFIELD                                        
U|                         Blake!                                                     
O|
N|               Blake begins to move faster, setting a punishing pace. Boots         
N|               clattering over the wooden boards.                                   
O|
C,E|                                   SCHOFIELD (CONT'D)                               
U|                         We just need to think about it-                            
C|                                   BLAKE                                            
U|                         -There’s nothing to think about.                           
U|                         It’s my big brother.                                       
O|
N|               Schofield runs to catch up, he falls in behind Blake,                
N|               breathing heavy.                                                     
O|
C|                                   SCHOFIELD                                        
U|                         We should at least wait till it’s                          
U|                         dark-                                                      
O|
O|                                                                (CONTINUED)
O|
O|
O|                                                                     12.        
O|
O|               CONTINUED:                                                
O|
C|                                   BLAKE                                            
U|                         Erinmore said to leave immediately.                        
C|                                   SCHOFIELD                                        
U|                         Erinmore’s never seen No Man’s                             
U|                         Land. We won’t make it ten yards.                          
U|                         If we just wait-                                           
O|
C|                                   BLAKE                                            
U|                         You heard him. He said the Boche                           
U|                         have gone.                                                 
O|
C|                                   SCHOFIELD                                        
U|                         Is that why he gave us grenades?                           
N|               The Second line runs through a small row of derelict railway         
N|               cottages. Braziers have been lit, men mill around queueing to        
N|               collect their rations.                                               
O|
N|               Schofield and Blake push themselves to the edge of the trench        
N|               to get around the crush.                                             
O|
N|               Blake is through and clear, but Schofield bumps into a               
N|               Sergeant.                                                            
O|
C|                                   SERGEANT                                         
U|                         Watch where you’re going!                                  
C|                                   SCHOFIELD                                        
U|                         Sorry.                                                     
O|
N|               Blake keeps pace, Schofield jogs to catch him.                       
O|
C,E|                                   SCHOFIELD (CONT'D)                               
U|                         All I’m saying is that we wait.                            
O|
C|                                   BLAKE                                            
U|                         Yes, you would say that, because                           
U|                         it’s not your brother, is it?                              
N|               Schofield moves alongside Blake again, grabs his arm.                
O|
C|                                   SCHOFIELD                                        
U|                         Look, the last time I was told the                         
U|                         Germans were gone, it didn’t end                           
U|                         well.                                                      
O|
N|               Blake shakes him off, and pushes his way forward, squeezing          
N|               in and out of the lines of traffic - His shoulder and pack           
N|               battering against MEN as he passes them.                             
O|
O|                                                                (CONTINUED)
O|
O|
O|                                                                     13.        
O|
O|               CONTINUED: (2)                                         
O|
C,E|                                   SCHOFIELD (CONT'D)                               
U|                         You don’t know, Blake, you weren’t                         
U|                         there.                                                     
N|               Ahead a group of men are bunched up collecting mail and              
N|               parcels from the post bag. Gumming up the trench.                    
O|
C|                                   BLAKE                                            
U|                         Excuse me... Excuse me!                                    
O|
N|               Blake and Schofield squeeze past them.                               
O|
