O|
N|               Blake looks at him with concern. Schofield nods that he’s            
N|               fine.                                                                
C|                                   SCHOFIELD                                        
U|                         Look for cover.                                            
O|
N|               Everything after here is unnatural land. Craters are gouged          
N|               out of the earth. There is a rise and fall to this stretch,          
N|               but no flow or reason to it.                                         
O|
N|               About a hundred yards from them, in the distance, is an              
N|               artificial horizon, something grey, mesh-like, stretching the        
N|               entire length of the land - The German Wire. Occasional dead         
N|               trees dot the land beyond.                                           
N|               Blake goes into the closest crater. He looks to Schofield,           
N|               some silent communication. Schofield’s eyes pull out a path          
N|               where there isn’t one.                                               
O|
