U|                         and listen well!                                           
O|
N|               Schofield spots the commanding voice, pushes through towards         
N|               the Lieutenant-                                                      
O|
C,E|                                   LIEUTENANT HUTTON (CONT'D)                       
U|                         On the first mark, A Company will                          
U|                         advance! B Company will then move                          
U|                         to the front line!                                         
O|
C|                                   SCHOFIELD                                        
U|                         Sir, I have a message from General                         
U|                         Erinmore!                                                  
C|                                   LIEUTENANT HUTTON                                
U|                         Who the fuck are you?                                      
O|
C|                                   SCHOFIELD                                        
U|                         The attack has been called off.                            
U|                         General Erinmore has called off the                        
U|                         attack.                                                    
O|
N|               The Lieutenant stares at Schofield, incredulous.                     
C|                                   LIEUTENANT HUTTON                                
U|                         Balls, man. We’re about to go over.                        
U|                         We’ve got them on the run.                                 
O|
C|                                   SCHOFIELD                                        
P|                             (frantic)                                              
U|                         You don’t! Please. Don’t send your                         
U|                         men over.                                                  
O|
C|                                   LIEUTENANT HUTTON                                
U|                         Get out of the way, Corporal -                             
O|
O|                                                                (CONTINUED)
O|
O|
O|                                                                     101.      
O|
O|               CONTINUED:                                                
O|
C|                                   SCHOFIELD                                        
U|                         These are direct orders from Army                          
U|                         command! Where is the Colonel                              
U|                         Mackenzie?                                                 
N|               Schofield brandishes his letter. Still wet from the river,           
N|               but legible. He looks like a madman. Hutton grabs him by the         
N|               lapels.                                                              
O|
C|                                   LIEUTENANT HUTTON                                
P|                             (furious)                                              
U|                         Jesus Christ, man! Go and see the                          
U|                         Captain!                                                   
N|               Hutton shoves him away. Schofield staggers on, pushing out of        
N|               the holding area. As he goes, we hear Hutton bellowing to his        
N|               men-                                                                 
O|
C,E|                                   LIEUTENANT HUTTON (CONT'D)                       
U|                         Now I want us up there quickly, you                        
U|                         understand? Do you understand!                             
O|
N|               Hutton’s men respond: ‘Yes, Sir!’ etc.                               
O|
N|               Schofield rushes through them and into -                             
O|
S|               EXT. 2ND FRONT LINE TRENCH - CONTINUOUS                              
O|
N|               The narrow trench is packed with more men.                           
O|
N|               This trench is hastily dug. Little more than a temporary             
N|               berm, perhaps five feet high. Hundreds of men crouch just            
N|               inside the trench wall, waiting, preparing.                          
O|
N|               He pushes past more men. And still more.                             
O|
C|                                   SERGEANT WRIGHT                                  
U|                         Sections 9 and 10 at the ready! We                         
U|                         will advance on the first whistle                          
U|                         blast!                                                     
N|               Schofield pushes forwards.                                           
O|
C|                                   SERGEANT GARDNER                                 
U|                         You must not slow down! If the man                         
U|                         next to you falls, keep moving!                            
U|                         Your orders are to break the lines -                       
O|
C|                                   SCHOFIELD                                        
U|                         Where is the Captain?                                      
O|
O|                                                                (CONTINUED)
O|
O|
O|                                                                     102.      
O|
O|               CONTINUED:                                                
O|
N|               Gardner nods to CAPTAIN IVINS, rocking back and forth, head          
N|               bowed.                                                               
C|                                   SERGEANT GARDNER                                 
U|                         He’s over there.                                           
O|
N|               Schofield gets to Ivins.                                             
O|
C|                                   SCHOFIELD                                        
U|                         Sir? Sir!                                                  
O|
N|               Ivins looks up at Schofield, he’s crying, muttering to               
N|               himself, terrified. Tears roll down his face.                        
C,E|                                   SCHOFIELD (CONT'D)                               
U|                         Captain, I have a message. This                            
U|                         attack is called off. You have to                          
U|                         stop, you have to stop -                                   
O|
N|               Before he can say more, the air vibrates. An impossibly loud         
N|               sound -                                                              
O|
N|               GERMAN ARTILLERY.                                                    
O|
N|               Shells scream overhead and then - a wall of noise.                   
O|
N|               The air seems to tremble.                                            
N|               SOLDIERS press themselves into the walls of the trench, take         
N|               cover wherever they can.                                             
O|
N|               The earth groans as the shells land. Pounding the earth all          
N|               around. Not yet zeroed in on the British Line.                       
O|
C|                                   CAPTAIN IVINS                                    
P|                             (Soundlessly)                                          
U|                         No. No. No.                                                
O|
N|               Schofield grabs Ivins.                                               
C|                                   SCHOFIELD                                        
P|                             (Shouting, soundless)                                  
U|                         Where is Colonel Mackenzie?                                
O|
N|               Men cover their ears and squeeze their skulls, but the sound         
N|               still drowns them. Captain Ivins has his hands over his ears.        
N|               Schofield tries to wrestle his arms away, so he can be heard.        
O|
C,E|                                   SCHOFIELD (CONT'D)                               
P|                             (Again, soundless)                                     
U|                         Where is Mackenzie?                                        
O|
O|                                                                (CONTINUED)
O|
O|
O|                                                                     103.      
O|
O|               CONTINUED: (2)                                         
O|
N|               No response. The noise is too much.                                  
N|               Some men push their heads against the front wall of the              
N|               trench, scream into the mud, all voices are lost. Others             
N|               cower into the earth.                                                
O|
N|               The noise is unbearable.                                             
O|
N|               Schofield leaves Ivins, moving faster through the line now as        
N|               men crouch and contort themselves low.                               
O|
N|               Schofield pushes forwards.                                           
O|
N|               Then, twenty yards behind Schofield - a direct hit.                  
N|               The concussion of the blast ripples along the narrow trench.         
O|
N|               The walls literally bleed earth and chalk.                           
O|
N|               In an instant IVINS, his men, the entire section of trench           
N|               they were in has vanished. They simply disappear -                   
O|
N|               Schofield is thrown forward, into a huddle of stunned men.           
O|
N|               Sound creeps back into the world, raspy screams over the             
N|               thunder of explosions. We can hear a voice in the distance.          
C,E|                                   SERGEANT GARDNER(O.S.)                           
U|                         Bearers! Stretcher bearers!                                
O|
N|               Schofield drags himself to his feet, keeps moving along the          
N|               trench.                                                              
O|
N|               German shells whistle through the air all around.                    
O|
N|               Schofield pushes his way along.                                      
O|
N|               Fountains of mud and iron burst in No Man’s Land, towering           
N|               into the sky, showering dirt and shrapnel onto the line.             
N|               Schofield doesn’t stop running, pushing through A and B              
N|               Companies.                                                           
O|
N|               The trench gets thinner, tapering in-                                
O|
N|               Schofield fights through the men now, running out of space,          
N|               running out of time.                                                 
O|
N|               The trench narrows until Schofield can’t get through the men.        
O|
N|               The PLATOONS have lost their form here, there are no gaps            
N|               between them, everyone is packed together in the chaos.              
O|
O|                                                                (CONTINUED)
O|
O|
O|                                                                     104.      
O|
O|               CONTINUED: (3)                                         
O|
N|               The German artillery is increasing now. Every moment is              
N|               rocked with noise. There is no space, no silence.                    
N|               Ahead of him, 100 yards down, the trench takes another direct        
N|               hit. But Schofield keeps moving towards it.                          
O|
N|               MEN flow away from the damage. Pushing their way towards             
N|               Schofield. Completely blocking the trench.                           
O|
N|               Schofield pushes forward until the trench becomes impassable.        
O|
N|               A wall of men, with nowhere to go.                                   
O|
N|               A burly Sergeant is ahead of him, brandishing a pistol,              
N|               yelling commands, trying to regain some sort of order, but           
N|               his words are lost in the roar of the shells.                        
C|                                   SERGEANT GUTHRIE                                 
U|                         GET BACK! Return to your sectors.                          
U|                         GET BACK! BACK! Hold fast!                                 
O|
N,I|               Schofield pushes past him, and finds the nearest C.O. -              
N,I|               LIEUTENANT RICHARDS. His eyes are on his men, revolver in            
N|               hand.                                                                
O|
C|                                   LIEUTENANT RICHARDS                              
U|                         SEVEN PLATOON! ONE MINUTE!                                 
N|               Schofield grabs at him, screams-                                     
O|
C|                                   SCHOFIELD                                        
U|                         Sir, I have orders to stop this                            
U|                         attack.                                                    
O|
N|               Richards wants to believe him.                                       
O|
C|                                   LIEUTENANT RICHARDS                              
U|                         What?                                                      
O|
C|                                   SCHOFIELD                                        
U|                         Where is Colonel Mackenzie?                                
C|                                   LIEUTENANT RICHARDS                              
U|                         He’s further up the line.                                  
O|
C|                                   SCHOFIELD                                        
U|                         How far?                                                   
O|
C|                                   LIEUTENANT RICHARDS                              
U|                         Three hundred yards. He’s in a cut                         
U|                         and cover.                                                 
O|
O|                                                                (CONTINUED)
O|
O|
O|                                                                     105.      
O|
O|               CONTINUED: (4)                                         
O|
N|               Both of them look around.                                            
C,E|                                   LIEUTENANT RICHARDS (CONT'D)                     
U|                         You’ll have to wait until the first                        
U|                         wave goes over.                                            
O|
C|                                   SCHOFIELD                                        
U|                         No! No, I can’t!                                           
O|
N|               Schofield turns and looks. More shells hit the trench. Chaos.        
N|               The way to Mackenzie is impassable. Panic mingles with               
N|               despair.                                                             
O|
N|               Richards turns back to his men.                                      
C|                                   LIEUTENANT RICHARDS                              
U|                         7 PLATOON! THIRTY SECONDS!                                 
O|
N|               Suddenly, Schofield climbs up onto the firing step...                
O|
N|               Richards turns and sees him.                                         
O|
C,E|                                   LIEUTENANT RICHARDS (CONT'D)                     
U|                         You can’t possibly make it that way                        
U|                         man, are you bloody insane?                                
O|
N|               300 yards. Open ground, utterly without cover. It may as well        
N|               be on the moon.                                                      
N|               Everything slows. Something in Schofield snaps.                      
O|
C,E|                                   LIEUTENANT RICHARDS (CONT'D)                     
U|                         What the hell are you doing, Lance                         
U|                         Corporal?                                                  
O|
N|               Schofield is on the top step...                                      
O|
N|               He stands.                                                           
O|
C,E|                                   LIEUTENANT RICHARDS (CONT'D)                     
U|                         NO, NO, NO, NO!                                            
N|               Richards and his men watch on in disbelief, as an unarmed            
N|               Schofield staggers out and into-                                     
O|
S|               EXT. NO MAN'S LAND - CONTINUOUS                                      
O|
N|               Schofield stumbles forwards. Shocked that he is now out in           
N|               the open.                                                            
O|
N|               Then he starts to run, picking up speed.                             
O|
O|                                                                (CONTINUED)
O|
O|
O|                                                                     106.      
O|
O|               CONTINUED:                                                
O|
N|               Now Schofield is sprinting full pelt, parallel to the trench-        
N|               His breath burns in and out, sawing in his ears                      
O|
N|               Schofield doesn’t stop.                                              
O|
N|               His legs thump over the earth.                                       
O|
N|               We hear the screech of the whistle. Three short blasts.              
O|
N|               The roar of hundreds of men follows-                                 
O|
N|               Schofield keeps sprinting to the western trench as now, SIX          
N|               HUNDRED SOLDIERS pour out of the British front line-                 
N|               Running out into No Man’s Land, and crossing in front and            
N|               behind Schofield.                                                    
O|
N|               Hundreds of soldiers, heading towards the German lines as he         
N|               keeps sprinting to the western trench.                               
O|
N|               The German guns now erupt again.                                     
O|
N|               Men fall in their dozens.                                            
O|
N|               Hundreds more pour over the top.                                     
N|               Schofield is only half way. He stumbles, falls. But picks            
N|               himself up and keeps on running.                                     
O|
N|               The whole world shakes on its axis as the shells land.               
O|
N|               The air thunders around him. The ground itself bursts and            
N|               rolls.                                                               
O|
N|               A Company are still pouring out into No Man’s Land.                  
O|
N|               Schofield is running, running.                                       
O|
N|               Through the hail of bullets and shells.                              
N|               Still running.                                                       
O|
N|               His lungs burn, his breath grates in his throat as he runs.          
O|
N|               Behind him, men continue to pour over the top.                       
O|
N|               Schofield sprints the final few feet and -                           
O|
N|               He jumps desperately into -                                          
O|
O|
O|                                                                     107.      
O|
S|               EXT. 2ND COMMAND TRENCH - CONTINUOUS                                 
N|               He tumbles and lands amongst the waiting men of B Company,           
N|               now in the breech.                                                   
O|
N|               Schofield careens through them and hits the ground hard.             
O|
N|               Men look down at him in horror. He brandishes his message as         
N,I|               a Captain, SANDBACH, closes in on him-                               
O|
C|                                   SCHOFIELD                                        
P|                             (Breathless)                                           
U|                         Colonel Mackenzie?                                         
