N|               direction of a dugout-                                               
O|
C|                                   CAPTAIN SANDBACH                                 
U|                         He’s in there.                                             
P|                             (he turns to his men)                                  
U|                         B Company two minutes!                                     
O|
N|               There is a lull in the shelling, the earth still rumbles             
N|               above them with the sounds of distant machine guns, but the          
N|               blasts have stopped.                                                 
O|
N|               Schofield runs, half limping, cutting through the men who are        
N|               about to be sent over the top, and pushes his way to the             
N|               entrance of a dugout.                                                
C|                                   SCHOFIELD                                        
U|                         Let me through!                                            
O|
C|                                   ORDERLY DIXON                                    
U|                         Hey, hey...!                                               
O|
C|                                   SCHOFIELD                                        
U|                         Let me through!                                            
O|
N,I|               Schofield drops down a few steps, a second orderly, BYRNE            
N|               grabs him. Schofield tries to get past.                              
C|                                   ORDERLY BYRNE                                    
P|                             (overlapping)                                          
U|                         What the hell do you think you’re                          
U|                         doing?                                                     
O|
C|                                   SCHOFIELD                                        
U|                         I have to get through. I have to                           
U|                         see Colonel Mackenzie!                                     
O|
O|                                                                (CONTINUED)
O|
O|
O|                                                                     108.      
O|
O|               CONTINUED:                                                
O|
C|                                   ORDERLY DIXON                                    
U|                         What are you doing?!                                       
C|                                   SCHOFIELD                                        
U|                         I have to stop this attack-                                
O|
N|               He pushes past Dixon and into-                                       
O|
S|               INT. MACKENZIE’S DUGOUT ANTE-ROOM - CONTINUOUS                       
O|
N|               The two Orderlies have Schofield by the arms now. He has no          
N|               strength left to fight them.                                         
N,I|               His voice is lost in melee, as CAPTAIN RYLANDS sweeps past           
N|               him and in-                                                          
O|
C|                                   CAPTAIN RYLANDS                                  
U|                         Colonel, we’ve seen flares, the men                        
U|                         on the left flank have made it to                          
U|                         the German Line-                                           
O|
C|                                   SCHOFIELD                                        
U|                         Colonel!                                                   
O|
C|                                   ORDERLY DIXON                                    
U|                         Hold him!                                                  
C|                                   SCHOFIELD                                        
U|                         Colonel!                                                   
O|
N|               The Orderlies haul him out of the dugout.                            
O|
S|               EXT. 2ND COMMAND TRENCH - CONTINUOUS                                 
O|
N|               Schofield struggles wildly against the orderlies, they have          
N|               him pinned against the trench wall.                                  
O|
C|                                   SCHOFIELD                                        
U|                         Listen to me, listen to me! I have                         
U|                         a letter! I need to see Colonel                            
U|                         MacKenzie!                                                 
N|               The Orderlies yell over him.                                         
O|
C|                                   ORDERLY BYRNE                                    
U|                         There’s no bloody way you’re                               
U|                         getting in there, mate!                                    
O|
N|               Captain Rylands exits the dugout and bellows down the sector         
N|               to two Sergeants.                                                    
O|
O|                                                                (CONTINUED)
O|
O|
O|                                                                     109.      
O|
O|               CONTINUED:                                                
O|
C|                                   CAPTAIN RYLANDS                                  
U|                         Sergeant! Send the next wave!                              
N|               The Sergeants yell back in the affirmative from further down         
N|               the line.                                                            
O|
C|                                   SCHOFIELD                                        
U|                         NO!                                                        
O|
N|               With the last of his strength, Schofield throws his elbow            
N|               into the stomach of one of the orderlies. He breaks away from        
N|               them and into-                                                       
O|
S|               INT. MACKENZIE'S DUGOUT - CONTINUOUS                                 
O|
N|               Schofield careens into the room. A huddle of OFFICERS are            
N|               inside, their backs to him. A commanding voice emanates from         
N|               among them.                                                          
O|
C,E|                                   COLONEL MACKENZIE (O.S.)                         
U|                         Tell Ivins and Murphy to direct                            
U|                         their men to the left flank.                               
U|                         Concentrate everything there.                              
O|
C|                                   SCHOFIELD                                        
U|                         COLONEL MACKENZIE!                                         
N|               The officers turn on Schofield, parting as they do. In the           
N,I|               centre, staring straight at him, is COLONEL MACKENZIE, 40s.          
O|
N|               Mackenzie stands ramrod straight, and is immaculately turned         
N|               out, despite the chaos surrounding him. He has a small scar          
N|               across his left eye.                                                 
O|
C,E|                                   SCHOFIELD (CONT'D)                               
P|                             (in a rush)                                            
U|                         Sir, this attack is not to go                              
U|                         ahead! You’ve been ordered to stop.                        
U|                         You have to stop.                                          
