U|                         Who the hell are you?                                      
O|
C|                                   SCHOFIELD                                        
U|                         Lance Corporal Schofield, Sir. 8th.                        
U|                         I have orders from General Erinmore                        
U|                         to call off this attack.                                   
O|
N|               Schofield offers up the letter. The other Officers all react.        
N|               But Mackenzie doesn’t take it.                                       
O|
O|                                                                (CONTINUED)
O|
O|
O|                                                                     110.      
O|
O|               CONTINUED:                                                
O|
C|                                   COLONEL MACKENZIE                                
U|                         You’re too late, Lance Corporal.                           
C|                                   SCHOFIELD                                        
U|                         Sir, these orders are from Army                            
U|                         Command. You have to read them.                            
O|
N|               He holds out the letter to Mackenzie. A damp scrap of paper.         
O|
N,I|               A Major, HEPBURN, is listening closely.                              
O|
C|                                   MAJOR HEPBURN                                    
U|                         Shall we hold back the second wave,                        
U|                         Sir?                                                       
C|                                   COLONEL MACKENZIE                                
U|                         No, Major. Hesitate now and we                             
U|                         lose. Victory is five hundred yards                        
U|                         away.                                                      
O|
N|               Mackenzie is resolute.                                               
O|
C|                                   SCHOFIELD                                        
U|                         Sir...Sir! Please read the letter.                         
O|
C|                                   COLONEL MACKENZIE                                
U|                         I have heard it all before.                                
U|                         I’m not going to wait until dusk,                          
U|                         or for fog. I’m not calling back my                        
U|                         men, only to send them out there                           
U|                         again tomorrow. Not when we’ve got                         
U|                         the bastards on the run. This is                           
U|                         their last stand.                                          
C|                                   SCHOFIELD                                        
U|                         The German’s planned this, Sir.                            
U|                         They’ve been planning it for                               
U|                         months. They want you to attack.                           
U|                         Read the letter.                                           
N|               This catches MacKenzie’s attention. He nods to Major Hepburn:        
N|               get the letter.                                                      
O|
N|               Hepburn takes the letter from Schofield, hands it to Colonel         
N|               MacKenzie.                                                           
O|
N|               MacKenzie opens it. Reads.                                           
O|
N|               His face utterly impassive. Inscrutable.                             
O|
N|               Schofield waits.                                                     
O|
O|                                                                (CONTINUED)
O|
O|
O|                                                                     111.      
O|
O|               CONTINUED: (2)                                         
O|
C|                                   COLONEL MACKENZIE                                
U|                         Major.                                                     
C|                                   MAJOR HEPBURN                                    
U|                         Yes, Sir.                                                  
O|
N|               A horrible moment of silence. Everything hangs on this.              
O|
C|                                   COLONEL MACKENZIE                                
U|                         Stand them down.                                           
O|
C|                                   MAJOR HEPBURN                                    
U|                         Yes, Sir.                                                  
N|               Schofield closes his eyes. Relief floods his body.                   
O|
N|               The Major runs from the dugout, a blast of whistles from the         
N|               outside - a signal to stop.                                          
O|
N|               Mackenzie addresses his other officers.                              
O|
C|                                   COLONEL MACKENZIE                                
U|                         Call up the orderlies. Tend the                            
U|                         wounded. Hold the line in case they                        
U|                         counter.                                                   
O|
C|                                   OFFICERS                                         
U|                         Yes, Sir.                                                  
N|               The Officers empty out of the dugout. Noises of orders being         
N|               shouted and whistles being blown seep in from outside.               
O|
N|               A long beat. Schofield senses Mackenzie moving closer to him.        
N|               They are now alone.                                                  
O|
N|               Mackenzie speaks quietly.                                            
O|
C|                                   COLONEL MACKENZIE                                
U|                         I hoped today might be a good day.                         
U|                         Hope is a dangerous thing.                                 
N|               Schofield stands stock still.                                        
O|
C,E|                                   COLONEL MACKENZIE (CONT'D)                       
U|                         That’s it for now. Then next week,                         
U|                         Command will send a different                              
U|                         message. Attack at dawn.                                   
O|
N|               Mackenzie looks him in the eye.                                      
O|
O|                                                                (CONTINUED)
O|
O|
O|                                                                     112.      
O|
O|               CONTINUED: (3)                                         
O|
C,E|                                   COLONEL MACKENZIE (CONT'D)                       
U|                         There is only one way this war                             
U|                         ends. Last man standing.                                   
N|               Mackenzie looks him up and down.                                     
O|
C,E|                                   COLONEL MACKENZIE (CONT'D)                       
U|                         Have someone see to your wounds.                           
O|
N|               Schofield is frozen.                                                 
O|
