U|                         Well, knowing Lieutenant Blake he                          
U|                         would have gone over with his men.                         
U|                         He was in the first wave.                                  
O|
C|                                   SCHOFIELD                                        
U|                         How could I find him, Sir?                                 
O|
O|                                                                (CONTINUED)
O|
O|
O|                                                                     113.      
O|
O|               CONTINUED: (4)                                         
O|
C|                                   MAJOR HEPBURN                                    
U|                         You can try the casualty clearing                          
U|                         station, behind the line.                                  
U|                         Otherwise...                                               
N|               Beat.                                                                
O|
C|                                   SCHOFIELD                                        
U|                         Thank you, Sir.                                            
O|
C,E|                                   CORPORAL CAIRNS (O.S.)                           
U|                         Major Hepburn, Sir!                                        
O|
N|               He leaves. A beat while Schofield orientates himself. Then he        
N|               turns and walks out into -                                           
O|
S|               EXT. 2ND TRENCH - CONTINUOUS                                         
O|
N|               The sounds of the wounded and the dying as they pass. The            
N|               German guns have stopped for now. A brief pause.                     
O|
N|               Schofield walks along the line.                                      
O|
N|               The B, C and D Companies are gathered, pulling in the                
N|               survivors, carrying dying and wounded men along the trench.          
N|               Lifting them by hand where they have no stretchers.                  
N|               Schofield continues along. Searching for officers, for               
N|               Lieutenant Blake. No one looks at him. No one sees him. He           
N|               slips past them, a ghost.                                            
O|
S|               EXT. SHATTERED COMMS TRENCH - CONTINUOUS                             
O|
N|               Schofield turns the corner, and pushes his way along the zig-        
N|               zag length of the trench.                                            
O|
N|               STRETCHER BEARERS push past him, pressing him against the            
N|               back wall as they pass with the wounded.                             
C|                                   SCHOFIELD                                        
U|                         Sergeant, I have to find Lieutenant                        
U|                         Blake. Do you know where he is?                            
O|
C|                                   SERGEANT                                         
U|                         No.                                                        
O|
N|               Schofield follows them, up a slope, and emerging out into-           
O|
O|
O|                                                                     114.      
O|
S|               EXT. MEADOW - CONTINUOUS                                             
N|               An impromptu field station, where several overwhelmed MEDICAL        
N|               OFFICERS, CHAPLAINS and ORDERLIES from the RAMC tend to the          
N|               wounded.                                                             
O|
N|               Schofield moves to the tent.                                         
O|
C|                                   SCHOFIELD                                        
U|                         Sir, is Lieutenant Blake here?                             
O|
C|                                   MEDICAL OFFICER                                  
U|                         No idea.                                                   
P|                             (beat)                                                 
U|                         Move along Corporal.                                       
N|               Schofield walks through the tent, scanning the wounded.              
N|               Looking at the faces, the bodies.                                    
O|
C|                                   MEDICAL OFFCIER                                  
U|                         If you can walk, move to the triage                        
U|                         area.                                                      
O|
N|               None of the men are officers, none could be Blake’s brother.         
O|
C|                                   SCHOFIELD                                        
U|                         Lieutenant Blake! Blake?! Has                              
U|                         anyone seen Lieutenant Blake?                              
N|               He moves through a tent of gravely wounded men. The terrible         
N|               sounds of the dying. None are Blake’s brother.                       
O|
N|               Schofield moves outside. He finally stands still, hopeless.          
N|               Sick with his failure.                                               
O|
C,E|                                   LIEUTENANT (O.S)                                 
U|                         Now come on boys. He’s taken one in                        
U|                         the leg. He’s lost a lot of blood.                         
O|
N|               Schofield turns to see an Officer. He is following a                 
N|               stretcher bearer into the field station from the opposite            
N|               direction.                                                           
N|               Schofield stares at the man’s back. The sound of his voice.          
N|               Just an instinct...                                                  
O|
C|                                   SCHOFIELD                                        
U|                         Lieutenant Blake?                                          
O|
N|               The Officer stops and turns to him. His similarity to his            
N|               brother takes Schofield’s breath away.                               
O|
O|                                                                (CONTINUED)
O|
O|
O|                                                                     115.      
O|
O|               CONTINUED:                                                
O|
C|                                   LIEUTENANT BLAKE                                 
U|                         Yes.                                                       
N|               Schofield is shaky on his feet. He sways a bit, staring at           
N|               him.                                                                 
O|
C,E|                                   LIEUTENANT BLAKE (CONT'D)                        
U|                         Do you need medical assistance?                            
O|
C|                                   SCHOFIELD                                        
U|                         No, Sir. I’m from the 8th.                                 
O|
C|                                   LIEUTENANT BLAKE                                 
U|                         What the hell are you doing here?                          
C|                                   SCHOFIELD                                        
U|                         I was sent here to deliver a                               
U|                         message--                                                  
O|
N|               Recognition plays on Blake’s face, he smiles at the mention          
N|               of his brother’s brigade, moves towards Schofield.                   
O|
C|                                   LIEUTENANT BLAKE                                 
U|                         The 8th? You must know my brother.                         
O|
C|                                   SCHOFIELD                                        
U|                         I was sent here with him.                                  
C|                                   LIEUTENANT BLAKE                                 
U|                         Tom’s here? Where is he?                                   
O|
N|               Schofield looks at him. Blake’s smile slowly drops. A pause.         
O|
C|                                   SCHOFIELD                                        
U|                         It was very quick.                                         
O|
N|               Blake takes it in.                                                   
O|
C,E|                                   SCHOFIELD (CONT'D)                               
U|                         I’m sorry.                                                 
N|               Blake nods, wordless. Schofield goes into his tunic pocket,          
N|               pulls out Blake’s possessions. There is blood on them. The           
N|               elder Blake’s face is ashen as he takes them. His eyes fill          
N|               with tears.                                                          
O|
C|                                   LIEUTENANT BLAKE                                 
U|                         What’s your name?                                          
O|
C|                                   SCHOFIELD                                        
U|                         Schofield, Sir.                                            
O|
O|                                                                (CONTINUED)
O|
O|
O|                                                                     116.      
O|
O|               CONTINUED: (2)                                         
O|
N|               Blake nods. He looks down at his brother’s possessions in his        
N|               hands.                                                               
C|                                   LIEUTENANT BLAKE                                 
U|                         I’m sorry... what?                                         
O|
C|                                   SCHOFIELD                                        
U|                         It’s Schofield, Sir. William                               
U|                         Schofield. Will.                                           
O|
C|                                   LIEUTENANT BLAKE                                 
U|                         Well, you need some food. Get                              
U|                         yourself to the mess tent.                                 
N|               Beat. Schofield turns to leave. Then -                               
O|
C|                                   SCHOFIELD                                        
U|                         If I may, I’d like to write to your                        
U|                         mother. Tell her that Tom wasn’t                           
U|                         alone.                                                     
O|
C|                                   LIEUTENANT BLAKE                                 
U|                         Of course.                                                 
O|
N|               Schofield searches for something to say.                             
O|
C|                                   SCHOFIELD                                        
U|                         He was...he was a good man. Always                         
U|                         telling funny stories.                                     
N|               Blake nods. It doesn’t seem enough.                                  
O|
N|               Then Schofield finds the right words.                                
O|
C,E|                                   SCHOFIELD (CONT'D)                               
U|                         He saved my life.                                          
O|
N|               Schofield reaches out to shake his hand. Blake takes it. They        
N|               are still for a second.                                              
C|                                   LIEUTENANT BLAKE                                 
U|                         I am glad you were with him.                               
P|                             (Then)                                                 
U|                         Thank you, Will.                                           
O|
N|               Schofield nods. He turns and walks away.                             
O|
N|               He is like a sleepwalker. Unsure of where to go.                     
O|
N|               He moves away from the makeshift Aid Post and into the meadow        
N|               beyond.                                                              
O|
O|                                                                (CONTINUED)
O|
O|
O|                                                                     117.      
O|
O|               CONTINUED: (3)                                         
O|
N|               The grass sways in the breeze. This place is beginning to            
N|               turn gold in the morning sun. Schofield drifts through it.           
N|               The noise of the horror behind him gradually fades.                  
O|
N|               Ahead, on the plain, an oak tree towers. Untouched. On the           
N|               high branches, leaves dance in the wind.                             
O|
N|               Schofield walks towards it. He sits on the far side of it,           
N|               his back to the trunk. The land stretches out ahead of him in        
N|               the early light.                                                     
O|
N|               He listens to the wind in the leaves. Birdsong.                      
N|               He undoes his breast pocket. He pulls out the small tobacco          
N|               tin. He stares at it.                                                
O|
N|               He takes a deep breath and opens it. Two photographs.                
O|
N|               Schofield lifts them out, looks at them:                             
O|
N|               TWO YOUNG GIRLS, his daughters. They smile at the camera.            
O|
N|               He looks at the other - his WIFE.                                    
O|
N|               He turns the photo over.                                             
N|               On the back, her handwriting:                                        
O|
N|               “Come back to us.”                                                   
O|
N|               He stares at it for a long beat.                                     
O|
N|               The pain on his face ebbs into longing. Love.                        
O|
N|               He closes his eyes and feels the sun on his face.                    
O|
M|               THE END.                                                             
O|
M|                           FOR LANCE CORPORAL ALFRED H. MENDES                      
O|
M|                          1ST BATTALION, KING’S ROYAL RIFLE CORPS                   
O|
